    "lawCode": "Amd §1210, Tax L",
    "lawSection": "Tax Law",
    "memo": " BILL NUMBER:  S4628\n\n TITLE OF BILL :\nAn act to amend the tax law, in relation to extending the\nauthorization of the county of Cayuga to impose an additional one\npercent of sales and compensating use taxes\n\n\n PURPOSE OF BILL :\nThis bill authorizes the County of Cayuga to extend one percent sales\ntax through 2011.\n\n SUMMARY OF SPECIFIC PROVISIONS :\nThis bill extends to the County of Cayuga's current one percent sales\ntax by amending the starting date from December 1, 2007 to December 1,\n2009. It also amends the ending date from November 30, 2009 to\nNovember 30, 2011.\n\n JUSTIFICATION :\nThe Cayuga County legislature has requested legislation to extend the\nCounty sales tax which is set to expire on December 1, 2009.\n\n PRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY :\nNew bill.\n\n FISCAL IMPLICATIONS :\nNone to the State.\n\n EFFECTIVE DATE :\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
